cancer treatment requires aggressive  intervention but some drugs such as mono  methyl or is that in E a too toxic for  systemic administration because they  damage healthy cells as well as tumor  cells however attaching the drug to an  antibody targeting a surface protein  highly expressed on tumor cells can  prevent collateral damage different  linkers can be used to attach a drug to  an antibody these linkers are designed  to break down and release active drug  only after antibody drug conjugate  enters the tumor cell  this allows drugs to be activated only  at the tumor site  unfortunately certain factors can weigh  lay the conjugate before it gets there  first the linker can break releasing the  drug from the antibody prematurely the  free drug can then kill healthy normal  cells leading to a variety of side  effects including peripheral neuropathy  to prevent this efforts to engineer more  stable linkers less likely to break are  underway  second healthy cells can ingest antibody  drug conjugate  in most cases conjugates are ultimately  recycled back out of the cell without  causing damage  conjugates that are not efficiently  recycled can kill the cells in which  they're retained a small percentage of  the antibody drug conjugates ultimately  reached the tumor but even conjugates  that reach the tumor may not kill tumor  cells for example if the cell doesn't  internalize the conjugate the drug can't  kill the cell efforts are underway to  ensure that protein selected as new  conjugate targets get internalized into  the cell in successful therapy tumor  cells internalize sufficient numbers of  conjugates  once inside the cell conjugate linkers  may be broken for example by lysosomal  enzymes active drug then enters the  cytoplasm inflicting lethal damage one  common mechanism to kill cells is to  inhibit assembly of microtubules which  are essential for cell division  two missiles that cannot divide die by  apoptosis active drug released from  dying tumor cells can kill nearby cells  including other tumor cells and stromal  cells antibody drug conjugates target  the toxic effects of chemo therapeutic  drugs to tumor cells thereby minimizing  the type of collateral damage that leads  to unwanted side-effects  you
 

